WEBVTT


00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.700
www. opensubtitles. org
- Omerta -


00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.000
Well, I'm just a smalltown cop,
Mostly I give out parking tickets.


00:00:26.035 --> 00:00:28.000
<i>I don't wanna talk about your work.</i>


00:00:28.035 --> 00:00:31.300
Ok... How are things in L.A.?


00:00:31.335 --> 00:00:32.265
<i>Jesse...</i>


00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.100
- Why'd you call me
at the office, Jenn?


00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.600
<i>I don't want you to call me tonight.</i>


00:00:39.635 --> 00:00:41.065
Ok.


00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.000
<i>Actually, I don't think
we should talk for a while.</i>


00:00:44.035 --> 00:00:45.967
How long, a while?


00:00:46.002 --> 00:00:47.900
<i>I don't know.</i>


00:00:47.935 --> 00:00:50.065
Ok.


00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.100
<i>So, now it's coming over.</i>


00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.800
<i>He thinks it's strange
that we still talk every night.</i>


00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.300
Was he there last night?


00:01:00.335 --> 00:01:02.317
<i>Yes.</i>


00:01:02.352 --> 00:01:04.300
Ok.


00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.900
<i>Do you understand?</i>


00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:09.865
No.


00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.600
<i>Are you alright?</i>


00:01:11.635 --> 00:01:12.565
Yeah...


00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:18.600
<i>Jesse... Thank you.</i>


00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.800
Things get this slow
when Lou was Chief?


00:01:38.835 --> 00:01:41.500
All the time. How's your wife?


00:01:41.535 --> 00:01:43.200
Ex-wife, Rose.


00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.000
- The Rabid skunk has benn dispatched.
- How?


00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.065
D'Angelo shot him.


00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.365
- Ok.
- D'Angelo was not happy...


00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.965
- What did he say?
- He said "Why it is always my fault?"


00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.700
Hey, I didn't say it was his fault,
I just said I was blaming him for it.


00:01:58.735 --> 00:02:00.165
He thinks you pick on him.


00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.402
Well, I don't like him.


00:02:01.403 --> 00:02:03.632
If you don't like him,
why don't you fire him?


00:02:03.835 --> 00:02:07.865
I'm not gonna fire him,
I'm gonna wear him down.


00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:11.065
Wednesday is your town council meeting.
Oh, I'm gonna be late tommorrow...


00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.494
I have to take Brian to the orthodontist.


00:02:12.495 --> 00:02:15.295
And Edwin says the Civil War
Memorial was falling down.


00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:16.827
He's watering too much.


00:02:16.828 --> 00:02:18.728
Well, he wants the square to
look good for the Fall Regatta.


00:02:18.735 --> 00:02:20.065
- Did you tell him?
- Yes.


00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.500
- What did he say?
- He wants to know, how you know?


00:02:22.535 --> 00:02:25.800
I'm the police chief, I know everything.


00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.950
They said it might be vandalism.


00:02:27.985 --> 00:02:29.800
Tell them he's watering to much.


00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.265
- Brahms.
- Excuse me?


00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:02.550
I'm Hilda Evans, Chief Stone.


00:03:02.585 --> 00:03:05.765
How's the drinking thing going?


00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:10.100
Small town. Ever since people heard
that you were drunk on your job interview...


00:03:10.135 --> 00:03:11.865
...there's been concern.


00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.900
Actually I drank too much the night before.
I just made the mistake...


00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.665
...of having one in the
morning to steady up.


00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:22.800
Brahms. When I'm feeling troubled,
I sit in my favourite chair...


00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:26.500
...put my head back, and listen to Brahms.


00:03:26.535 --> 00:03:31.000
I find it comforting. Enough said.


00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.300
Wake up!


00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.965
I know you can hear me.


00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.600
Doctor says your wound's
completely healed.


00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.965
Believe it or not,
Melbourne, Australia.


00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.000
A man left comatose for over
ten years, suddenly sat bolt...


00:04:08.035 --> 00:04:11.300
...upright and said
"I'll have a cappuccino."


00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.700
Well, everything happens
at once, Suitcase.


00:04:21.735 --> 00:04:23.800
Things are really jumping in Paradise.


00:04:23.835 --> 00:04:25.800
Rampant crime.


00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.018
I just heard at
the weekly briefing...


00:04:28.019 --> 00:04:31.427
... that there's a drug ring
trying to set up in our town.


00:04:31.462 --> 00:04:34.900
I could use a little backup!


00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:41.700
Suit, we're four people police force.
With Molly out, I got to retrain Rose...


00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.200
The town council wants me to replace you.


00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.165
"It was bitter cold"


00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.700
"The wind in his face made it difficult
to grasp the shape before him. "


00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.800
"The bow of the yacht cut through
the sea, needly cleaving the water... "


00:05:12.835 --> 00:05:14.965
"... into mirror image waves. "


00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.218
"Now he saw the ship
with in its full glory..."


00:05:18.219 --> 00:05:23.419
"...80 feet at least,
mahogany hull in full sail, dark and silent. "


00:05:23.535 --> 00:05:26.400
"A latter day Flying Dutchman. "


00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.000
ROBERT B. PARKER'S
JESSE STONE


00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.500
SEA CHANGE


00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.500
Nice car.


00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:21.400
Are you giving me a ticket?


00:08:21.435 --> 00:08:23.267
- It depends.
- On what?


00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:25.065
If this is your car...


00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.200
You don't hink I can own a car like this?


00:08:27.235 --> 00:08:29.300
- I didn't say that.
- It's not mine.


00:08:29.335 --> 00:08:32.365
Then I'm not giving you a ticket.


00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.100
Look, the owner's
just been in a week...


00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.000
- ...He came up for Race Week.
- Race Week.


00:08:38.035 --> 00:08:40.617
Race Week is good for local business, right?


00:08:40.652 --> 00:08:43.200
- It is.
- Ok, why give him the ticket?


00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.665
The curb is red.


00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.465
What if it were my car?


00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:51.300
I'm still give it a ticket,
but with infinitely more regret.


00:08:51.335 --> 00:08:54.665
- So, are you feeling regret?
- A little.


00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:58.300
Alright, it's not hard to fix that.
Tear it up!


00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.565
No.


00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.000
You gonna get me
in trouble, don't you.


00:09:03.035 --> 00:09:03.965
No.


00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.700
And you are feeling regret.


00:09:06.735 --> 00:09:09.100
Yes.


00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.865
Don't you have anything better to do...


00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:20.500
...then spend your time
with writing parking tickets?


00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:23.500
No.


00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.665
<i>Hi jesse, it's Jenn.</i>


00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:58.000
<i>I guess you are left,
I'll call you at the office.</i>


00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:26.300
- Hello?
- It's me.


00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.665
What's wrong?


00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:32.700
Nothing, I just wanted to see
how you're doing, Molly.


00:12:32.735 --> 00:12:35.417
Fine... You?


00:12:35.452 --> 00:12:38.065
I woke you up.


00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.465
<i>Oh no, you didn't, I'm...</i>


00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:42.200
...too uncomfortable to sleep.


00:12:42.235 --> 00:12:45.900
What time is it?


00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:52.600
9 o'clock in L.A.
How is Jenn?


00:12:52.635 --> 00:12:54.500
Fine.


00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:56.150
You Ok?


00:12:56.185 --> 00:12:57.565
<i>Yes.</i>


00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:59.700
Would you tell me, if you're worrying?


00:12:59.735 --> 00:13:01.065
No.


00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:03.900
<i>There's a lot of people
care about you, Jesse.</i>


00:13:03.935 --> 00:13:05.500
Including you?


00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:07.800
Especially me.


00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:10.600
So you think you gonna
have the kid early?


00:13:10.635 --> 00:13:13.700
Hopefully not too early.


00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.765
How's Rose doing?


00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:17.500
She's a little rusty,
but she's doing fine.


00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.100
Did you see Suitcase today?


00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.200
<i>Every day.</i>


00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.100
Did you give him my love?


00:13:23.135 --> 00:13:25.600
I forgot.


00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:28.265
Oh, did you have the test?


00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:33.600
Oh, the baby's fine.
I'm what's termed the "high risk" mother.


00:13:33.635 --> 00:13:36.000
Means "old".


00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:41.700
Jesse, I need to get some sleep.


00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:48.100
- I woke you up.
- Will you call me tomorrow?


00:13:48.135 --> 00:13:50.800
Ugh, sure.


00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:06.500
- So, nobody called?
- I don't do phones.


00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.050
- You go now?
- Aham, in a while.


00:16:12.085 --> 00:16:14.700
'Cause we're almost
out of coffee.


00:16:14.735 --> 00:16:17.100
I think you should get some.


00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.400
Alright, I'll buy it.


00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:28.100
- Ugh, Skipper, I...
- Not today, D'Angelo.


00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:44.800
- Are you alright?
- I'm fine.


00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:56.200
You can't come every couple of months,
and expect to get anything done.


00:16:56.235 --> 00:16:59.965
I've been busy.
Fighting crime.


00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:04.600
- It's small town, What do you wait?
- What I've come to expect.


00:17:04.635 --> 00:17:07.765
You take a job you're overqualified for.


00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:11.700
You're good at what you do, so you
stir the pot up comes a couple of rats


00:17:11.735 --> 00:17:15.800
but for all intents and purposes,
nothing happens here.


00:17:15.835 --> 00:17:19.517
You know what I'm
talking about, you're a cop.


00:17:19.552 --> 00:17:23.200
- Yeah, but I quit.
- Because it made you drink?


00:17:23.235 --> 00:17:26.500
I think that's called "projection".


00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:31.650
- So... You called me.
- In a moment of weakness.


00:17:31.685 --> 00:17:36.100
Is that happened last night?
A moment of weakness?


00:17:36.135 --> 00:17:38.765
No.


00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:43.500
- Did you talk to you ex-wife?
- You think that's what makes me drink.


00:17:43.535 --> 00:17:47.465
- Do you drink when you work?
- No.


00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:51.000
- So then you drink when you get home.
- I have two drinks.


00:17:51.035 --> 00:17:55.165
- Did you had two drinks last night?
- No.


00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:57.965
- And did you talk to your ex-wife?
- I talk to her every night.


00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:03.600
- And did you speak with her last night?
- Are you sensing a breakthrough?


00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:14.000
Do you drink, when you're
involved in a serious crime?


00:18:14.035 --> 00:18:16.265
- No.
- Because?


00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:20.100
- It would be unprofessional.
- So you stop.


00:18:20.135 --> 00:18:23.765
- Yes.
- As long as you need to.


00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:27.200
- Yes.
- And how long do you need to?


00:18:27.235 --> 00:18:30.417
- It depends.
- On what?


00:18:30.452 --> 00:18:33.600
On how long I need to.


00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:39.800
If you've got nothing to do,
pal, find something to do.


00:18:39.835 --> 00:18:45.200
If it's not important,
make it important.


00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.550
Rose, where do we keep
the unsolved cases?


00:19:05.585 --> 00:19:08.100
You mean where do "I" keep
the unsolved cases?


00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.800
- What kind of cases?
- I want a homicide.


00:19:11.835 --> 00:19:16.600
There's three. 1905, 1923, and 1992.


00:19:16.635 --> 00:19:18.265
- You know?
- Yes...


00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:22.600
- How do you know?
- I'm the dispatcher, I know everything.


00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:27.800
Molly rearranged my files,
I rearrenged them back.


00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.665
1992.


00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:34.400
- You said you wanted to get in the field.
- Not in this field...


00:19:34.435 --> 00:19:36.965
- And you're sure you can find it.
- I'm sure...


00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:40.559
No other customers, just, uh, the bank guard...


00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:43.060
...Hasty Hathaway, and the bankteller.


00:19:43.135 --> 00:19:46.600
A robber takes the teller hostage,
uses her as a shield.


00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:48.496
The bank guard gets off
an errant shot...


00:19:48.497 --> 00:19:51.656
... as he's dragging her out
the door. Then they disappear.


00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:55.265
You know, in six months,
none of this is gonna be here,


00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:58.100
some guy bought up the whole point,
gonna put up forty houses...


00:19:58.135 --> 00:20:00.617
- Yeah, rich people from Boston...
- Do me a favor...


00:20:00.652 --> 00:20:03.100
Tell the town council not to
reassess and raise my taxes


00:20:03.135 --> 00:20:05.565
A tenuous relationship at best.


00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:08.600
Ever since our friend Hasty resigned.
They don't seem to understand...


00:20:08.635 --> 00:20:10.667
...why I was hired to begin with...


00:20:10.702 --> 00:20:12.665
but I will tell them just the same.


00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:17.300
Anyway, two years later some hunters find
the teller's body in her shallow grave.


00:20:17.335 --> 00:20:20.300
- Why are you so sure you can find it?
- It would be hard to forget.


00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:21.632
Because?


00:20:21.633 --> 00:20:25.833
I threw up all over the body,
first time I saw her.


00:20:25.868 --> 00:20:27.900
Well, that would be a reason.


00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:42.900
I'll have a cappucino.


00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:55.500
I threw up the first time
I found a body.


00:20:55.535 --> 00:20:57.365
That's comforting.


00:20:57.400 --> 00:21:00.000
And that's when Lou pulled you out of field?


00:21:00.035 --> 00:21:02.600
Yeah, well, he promoted me to dispatcher...


00:21:02.635 --> 00:21:05.100
- And this is the spot.
- Yeah.


00:21:05.135 --> 00:21:06.165
How you know?


00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.900
This is the rock I sat on after I threw up.


00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:15.000
- This about the right depth?
- Yeah.


00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.900
Oh my God! The grave is empty!


00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:25.000
Maybe that's because the body
was removed thirteen years ago.


00:21:25.035 --> 00:21:27.365
Jesse, what are we doing?


00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:30.600
We're waiting for a clue to pop up.


00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:35.665
We had this coroner in L.A.,
with that asian guy


00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:40.900
he recovered this body in her shallow grave,
just kept saying "Dig deeper! Dig deeper!"


00:21:40.935 --> 00:21:42.365
Because he was asian?


00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:44.665
No. Because he was stubborn.


00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:48.000
And anytime some would ask "why",
like you keep doing...


00:21:48.035 --> 00:21:50.500
...he'd say "because I'm a
stubborn asian guy".


00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:53.300
Why?


00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:57.800
That's not the point.
The point is...


00:21:57.835 --> 00:22:01.000
...he dug up the murder weapon.


00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:13.700
That was sloppy police work, Lou.


00:22:21.700 --> 00:22:23.300
Thank you.


00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:27.700
- She's afraid of me.
- Oh, she'll be okay.


00:22:28.300 --> 00:22:31.100
- Can I talk to her?
- She won't talk to you, Luther.


00:22:31.135 --> 00:22:33.565
- Because?
- Because she's afraid of you.


00:22:33.600 --> 00:22:36.800
- D'Angelo!
- So Luther, do you remember anything?


00:22:39.600 --> 00:22:42.700
I remember cookies.


00:22:43.900 --> 00:22:47.150
And I remember juice.
Cranberry juice.


00:22:47.185 --> 00:22:50.400
You were shot at the market, Luther.


00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:53.200
Oh.


00:22:55.300 --> 00:22:58.000
Anything new on the drug case, Lou?


00:22:58.100 --> 00:22:59.500
Excuse me?


00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:04.300
Anything new on the drug case?


00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:08.400
Not really.


00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:24.765
And no blood at the scene.


00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:26.765
Apparently not.
There is nothin in the report...


00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:30.200
No, a lot of things are in the report.
I know you're fond of your old boss...


00:23:30.235 --> 00:23:33.465
...but that report is a mess.
And what was the robber wearing?


00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:35.826
Jesse, I know these are
the robber's clothes.


00:23:35.827 --> 00:23:37.327
He didn't need the hostage anymore...


00:23:37.335 --> 00:23:41.100
...so he shot the teller, buried in a
shallow grave, changed his own clothes...


00:23:41.135 --> 00:23:42.965
...buried them, so he
wouldn't be recognized.


00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:45.600
Well, actually he buried his clothes,
and then he buried the teller...


00:23:45.635 --> 00:23:47.165
...doesn't it seem backwards to you?


00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:49.865
- I guess it could be...
- Lou should've found these.


00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:53.700
- He found the body, that's pretty big.
- Actually some hunter's found the body.


00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:57.065
And what d'you suppose
made these holes?


00:23:57.100 --> 00:24:00.400
- Ugh, fifteen years underground?
- Organic matter.


00:24:00.435 --> 00:24:03.600
How was the body ID-d?


00:24:03.800 --> 00:24:07.665
- Her mother.
- Not even dental records?


00:24:07.700 --> 00:24:12.700
"Mary Lewis came in, looked to the
body, and said 'that's my little girl' ".


00:24:14.900 --> 00:24:17.400
Excuse me.


00:24:21.400 --> 00:24:24.000
- I'm Chief Stone.
- My name's Sam Holton.


00:24:24.035 --> 00:24:26.600
My daughter Cathleen.


00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:32.400
Why don't we go on into my office.
Officer Gammon.


00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:38.400
We'd just passed Paradise Cove
when it happened.


00:24:38.435 --> 00:24:41.600
On one of those yachts
come up for Raceweek.


00:24:41.635 --> 00:24:43.217
What happened?


00:24:43.252 --> 00:24:44.800
I was raped.


00:24:45.600 --> 00:24:48.300
- Do you know who did it?
- The owner of the boat.


00:24:48.500 --> 00:24:52.100
- Do you know the name of the boat?
- The "Lady Jane".


00:24:52.135 --> 00:24:55.665
- Could you pick the owner out of a lineup?
- Yeah.


00:24:55.700 --> 00:25:00.600
Good. Officer Gammon will take the rest
of your report and then we'll look into it.


00:25:00.635 --> 00:25:02.900
Now if you excuse me...


00:25:06.900 --> 00:25:10.100
- Have you talked to your wife?
- Ex-wife.


00:25:10.800 --> 00:25:14.600
I'll take that as a "no".
I thought you spoke to her every night.


00:25:14.635 --> 00:25:17.465
- Not lately.
- Why not?


00:25:17.500 --> 00:25:21.000
- She's seeing someone.
- At night?


00:25:21.035 --> 00:25:23.465
- Yes.
- At your house?


00:25:23.500 --> 00:25:27.800
- Oh, yeah.
- How do you feel about that?


00:25:27.835 --> 00:25:31.700
Like I wanna kill him.


00:25:38.800 --> 00:25:44.300
Do you imagine her
with him, having sex?


00:25:47.600 --> 00:25:48.900
Yes.


00:25:49.600 --> 00:25:52.665
- Does she tell you about it?
- No.


00:25:52.700 --> 00:25:55.200
- So, in fact, you don't know
what she's doing.


00:25:55.235 --> 00:25:59.400
I don't know anything...


00:26:04.700 --> 00:26:07.800
So you invent it.


00:26:08.700 --> 00:26:12.300
How long have you been
inventing her life?


00:26:14.500 --> 00:26:18.700
- I'll take that as an "always".
- Not always.


00:26:19.100 --> 00:26:25.600
- Since the divorce?
- You're pretty good at this.


00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:29.100
How many year's it to
take to be a psychiatrist?


00:26:29.135 --> 00:26:32.200
- Ten.
- You got to go at medical school first.


00:26:33.300 --> 00:26:37.400
- I'd have a question for you.
- A medical question?


00:26:37.700 --> 00:26:43.700
- A medical slash-cop question.
- Is this important?


00:26:44.100 --> 00:26:46.000
I hope so.


00:26:46.300 --> 00:26:48.165
What's the question?


00:26:48.200 --> 00:26:51.600
Bugs go after organic
matter first, right?


00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:55.865
What kind of bugs?
What kind of organic matter?


00:26:55.900 --> 00:26:59.865
I have these clothes, and they've
been buried for about fifteen years...


00:26:59.900 --> 00:27:05.200
...and pretty deteriorated, but there
are two big holes - one on the shirt...


00:27:05.235 --> 00:27:10.500
...one on the jacket, and they
line up, with, I think it might be, blood.


00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:16.600
You know what I think?
I think you won't be drinking tonight.


00:27:31.800 --> 00:27:33.600
Who are you lookin' at?


00:27:53.700 --> 00:27:59.900
<i>Hi, jesse. It's Jenn. I guess you
already left. I'll call you at the office.</i>


00:28:03.200 --> 00:28:10.000
<i>Hi, jesse. It's Jenn. I guess you
already left. I'll call you at the office..</i>


00:29:05.100 --> 00:29:08.900
- So where is Stone?
- Town Council.


00:29:09.300 --> 00:29:12.800
- You interviewed the raped victim?
- Basically.


00:29:12.835 --> 00:29:16.265
- Don't you think he should've
been there? I mean...


00:29:16.300 --> 00:29:21.500
He's always the first one to work.
But he wasn't the other day.


00:29:21.535 --> 00:29:24.700
- That's correct.
- Why do you think that is?


00:29:26.200 --> 00:29:28.100
- You know what I think?
- Tony.


00:29:28.700 --> 00:29:30.900
I don't really care what you think.


00:29:31.700 --> 00:29:36.700
The rabid skunk is no longer a threat,
Officer D'Angelo expressed his regrets.


00:29:36.735 --> 00:29:40.265
Uh, sixty-three parking tickets,
fourteen traffic stops...


00:29:40.300 --> 00:29:44.100
...and Edwin claims the Civil War
Memorial has been vandalized.


00:29:44.135 --> 00:29:45.865
You don't think it has been?


00:29:45.900 --> 00:29:49.450
Maybe you could tell him
he's watering too much.


00:29:49.485 --> 00:29:53.000
- What about this rape case?
- What about it?


00:29:53.035 --> 00:29:55.865
- Anyone arrested?
- No.


00:29:55.900 --> 00:29:58.065
- Good...
- Rape out of season?


00:29:58.100 --> 00:30:01.165
All our merchants need Raceweek,
I don't need a scandal.


00:30:01.200 --> 00:30:02.277
I know that.


00:30:02.278 --> 00:30:04.878
The Fall Regatta brings in
a lot of revenue.


00:30:04.935 --> 00:30:07.500
Including your paycheck.


00:30:09.300 --> 00:30:13.300
- So how have you been?
- Fine.


00:30:13.335 --> 00:30:16.200
- No problems.
- No.


00:30:17.400 --> 00:30:20.400
No... personal issues?


00:30:23.300 --> 00:30:25.665
Anything we need to know about?


00:30:25.700 --> 00:30:30.500
Yes, my deputy doesn't want you to
reassess her house and raise her taxes.


00:30:46.300 --> 00:30:48.265
What are you looking at?


00:30:48.300 --> 00:30:52.000
I was admiring the rigging
on the "Lady Jane".


00:30:53.300 --> 00:30:55.465
What d'you use for bait?


00:30:55.500 --> 00:30:58.850
Bugs, worms, last night supper.


00:30:58.885 --> 00:31:02.200
- Catch much?
- Don't catch spit.


00:31:02.400 --> 00:31:03.200
- Plenty of fish, though.
- Yep.


00:31:06.200 --> 00:31:10.800
- Maybe you should just shoot 'em.
- The fish or the bank robber?


00:31:15.100 --> 00:31:16.700
You a good shot, Bob?


00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:18.100
I was certified


00:31:18.600 --> 00:31:21.000
expert with a pistol
in the Army.


00:31:21.100 --> 00:31:21.900
Which war?


00:31:22.200 --> 00:31:22.600
Korea.


00:31:23.900 --> 00:31:25.500
You a good shot now?


00:31:25.535 --> 00:31:26.500
I don't know.


00:31:27.200 --> 00:31:28.800
How old are you, Bob?


00:31:29.300 --> 00:31:29.900
76.


00:31:31.400 --> 00:31:34.000
You a good shot
when you were 61?


00:31:34.500 --> 00:31:35.700
I thought I was.


00:31:36.300 --> 00:31:39.700
You had to be qualified
to be a bank guard.


00:31:40.900 --> 00:31:45.000
Have you ever been in a hostage
situation, Chief Stone?


00:31:48.200 --> 00:31:48.800
Yes.


00:31:51.300 --> 00:31:53.000
Did you take the shot?


00:31:55.800 --> 00:31:56.400
Yes.


00:31:57.100 --> 00:31:57.800
So did I.


00:31:59.000 --> 00:32:02.700
I reached for my backup,
and I went to the door.


00:32:02.800 --> 00:32:05.000
I saw him in
my front sight.


00:32:06.100 --> 00:32:10.100
I figured he'd kill Rebecca
when he didn't need her.


00:32:10.900 --> 00:32:13.000
Well, you figured right, Bob.


00:32:13.400 --> 00:32:16.000
What caliber bullet
killed Rebecca?


00:32:20.100 --> 00:32:20.700
.38.


00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:23.100
That's what I was shooting.


00:32:23.700 --> 00:32:25.600
You don't think that I...


00:32:27.800 --> 00:32:30.400
No. And I don't
think you should.


00:32:33.100 --> 00:32:34.000
Why is that?


00:32:34.100 --> 00:32:36.700
Not healthy.
It will drive you to drink.


00:32:36.800 --> 00:32:37.700
Already did.


00:32:38.600 --> 00:32:40.800
Six years sober come December.


00:32:46.800 --> 00:32:48.600
And when did this happen?


00:32:48.635 --> 00:32:49.400
Four days ago.


00:32:49.500 --> 00:32:52.000
Cathleen, we have
no evidence of that.


00:32:52.100 --> 00:32:53.400
So you think I was lying?


00:32:53.500 --> 00:32:54.900
It doesn't mean you' re lying.


00:32:55.000 --> 00:32:56.600
It just means
there was no sperm.


00:32:56.700 --> 00:32:58.600
He was wearing
a rubber.


00:32:59.200 --> 00:33:02.000
I thought it was be best
if Cathleen


00:33:02.300 --> 00:33:03.600
and I discussed this.


00:33:03.700 --> 00:33:04.700
The rape test was inconclusive.


00:33:04.800 --> 00:33:07.600
Why don't you tell us the part
you didn't want your dad


00:33:07.700 --> 00:33:09.000
to hear, Cathleen?


00:33:10.300 --> 00:33:12.500
They made me do a striptease.


00:33:12.900 --> 00:33:13.800
Were you drinking?


00:33:13.900 --> 00:33:17.000
Yes. They said
I had to do a striptease


00:33:17.600 --> 00:33:20.000
or they wouldn't
take me back to shore.


00:33:20.100 --> 00:33:20.800
Who is they?


00:33:20.900 --> 00:33:23.700
The guy that raped me
and two other guys.


00:33:23.800 --> 00:33:25.700
They said
I had to strip.


00:33:25.800 --> 00:33:26.800
So you' re saying
they forced you?


00:33:26.900 --> 00:33:31.100
Yes. And then the guy who owned
the boat took me downstairs.


00:33:31.200 --> 00:33:33.400
I thought, you know, so
I could get dressed again,


00:33:33.500 --> 00:33:35.900
but he just threw me on the bed
and raped me.


00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:36.900
He was like an animal.


00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:38.600
Just threw me down
and jumped on me.


00:33:38.700 --> 00:33:40.300
But he wore a condom.


00:33:40.400 --> 00:33:40.865
Yes.


00:33:40.900 --> 00:33:44.700
Did he put that on just before
he jumped on you like an animal?


00:33:44.800 --> 00:33:46.100
Yeah. Just before.


00:33:46.800 --> 00:33:48.300
Was it in a packet?


00:33:48.400 --> 00:33:48.965
Yes.


00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:50.500
Did he have to open the packet?


00:33:50.600 --> 00:33:51.900
I don't remember.


00:33:59.000 --> 00:34:01.400
You think she's lying?
You don't think she was raped?


00:34:01.500 --> 00:34:02.700
I didn't say that.
Well, I think


00:34:02.800 --> 00:34:04.900
we can get a warrant.
Sure, we can get a warrant,


00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:06.100
but I don't want to.


00:34:06.200 --> 00:34:07.100
Since when
do you care


00:34:07.200 --> 00:34:08.100
what the Town
Council thinks?


00:34:08.200 --> 00:34:10.200
I don't.
But I do care about Paradise.


00:34:10.300 --> 00:34:12.400
You prosecute a rape case
in a resort town,


00:34:12.500 --> 00:34:14.500
all the cable news channels


00:34:14.600 --> 00:34:15.500
will live here.


00:34:15.600 --> 00:34:18.100
And no rape shield law
will protect that kid.


00:34:18.200 --> 00:34:19.700
Legally, she's not a kid.


00:34:19.800 --> 00:34:22.300
I think it's blood
on his clothes.


00:34:22.400 --> 00:34:23.200
Excuse me?


00:34:24.200 --> 00:34:27.800
I want to test
the robber's clothes for blood.


00:34:28.100 --> 00:34:30.400
So, after he
shot the teller,


00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:32.500
he dragged the body
to the grave


00:34:32.600 --> 00:34:33.800
and got blood on
his clothes. So what?


00:34:33.900 --> 00:34:37.000
So what? How much money
was taken in the robbery?


00:34:37.100 --> 00:34:40.100
Just the cash
that was in the bank: $24,000.


00:34:40.200 --> 00:34:41.300
Hardly worth a life.


00:34:41.400 --> 00:34:42.300
Jesse, what's the point?


00:34:42.400 --> 00:34:45.500
The point is, this isn't
just a robbery, Officer Gammon.


00:34:45.600 --> 00:34:46.700
It's a murder.


00:34:47.200 --> 00:34:48.600
And the guy got away with it.


00:34:48.700 --> 00:34:51.700
This report doesn't even
say whether she was shot


00:34:51.800 --> 00:34:53.300
from the front or the back.


00:34:53.400 --> 00:34:54.100
No, it doesn't.


00:34:54.200 --> 00:34:55.800
And I'm not happy
with the ID of the body.


00:34:55.900 --> 00:34:57.700
You don't want to run a DNA test.
I do.


00:34:57.800 --> 00:35:00.400
You don't think a mother could
recognize her own daughter?!


00:35:00.500 --> 00:35:02.100
Not after two years underground.


00:35:02.200 --> 00:35:03.900
She recognized the clothes.


00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:05.100
And where are they?


00:35:05.200 --> 00:35:06.100
Lieu returned


00:35:06.900 --> 00:35:08.100
the effects
to the family.


00:35:08.200 --> 00:35:09.800
Jesse, this stuff
isn't important!


00:35:09.900 --> 00:35:11.600
I think it is.
Why?


00:35:11.635 --> 00:35:13.300
Because I need it to be!


00:35:28.800 --> 00:35:32.100
What was the mother's
last known whereabouts?


00:35:32.200 --> 00:35:34.900
Sisters of Mercy
Hospital, up north.


00:35:35.300 --> 00:35:36.400
Jesse...


00:35:36.800 --> 00:35:39.000
I think DeAngelo went
to the Town Council.


00:35:39.100 --> 00:35:41.400
I would expect no less of him.


00:35:43.600 --> 00:35:45.200
They' re laying for you.


00:35:45.300 --> 00:35:46.400
The ugly truth of it, Rose,


00:35:46.500 --> 00:35:49.000
is it doesn't matter
a whole hell of a lot to me.


00:35:49.100 --> 00:35:52.700
Jesse, you need to concentrate
on the rape case.


00:35:58.300 --> 00:35:59.200
I know.


00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.100
You' re right.


00:36:02.300 --> 00:36:03.100
Thank you.


00:37:17.800 --> 00:37:18.400
Yes?


00:37:19.200 --> 00:37:21.900
I'm Jesse Stone,
the police chief in Paradise.


00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:24.100
You' re a long way from home.


00:37:24.200 --> 00:37:26.400
I was looking for Mary Lewis.


00:37:27.100 --> 00:37:28.700
Oh, my mom's resting.


00:37:29.700 --> 00:37:31.600
You look like your sister.


00:37:31.900 --> 00:37:33.800
Is this is about Rebecca?


00:37:35.000 --> 00:37:35.600
Yes.


00:37:36.200 --> 00:37:37.900
Oh, I'm... I'm sorry.


00:37:38.300 --> 00:37:40.300
I'm Leeann Lewis. Come in.


00:37:40.700 --> 00:37:41.500
Thank you.


00:37:50.400 --> 00:37:53.800
You can speak to her,
but she won't speak back.


00:37:53.900 --> 00:37:55.500
My mom had a stroke.


00:37:57.000 --> 00:37:58.200
Mama, this is...


00:37:59.700 --> 00:38:01.500
Jesse Stone,
Mrs. Lewis.


00:38:02.100 --> 00:38:03.500
I was just visiting


00:38:03.900 --> 00:38:04.800
with Leeann.


00:38:08.200 --> 00:38:10.200
Would you like some coffee?


00:38:11.600 --> 00:38:12.500
I would.


00:38:14.800 --> 00:38:17.000
Nice meeting you,
Mrs. Lewis.


00:38:25.700 --> 00:38:27.500
When did your mom
have the stroke?


00:38:27.600 --> 00:38:29.900
The day after she
identified Rebecca.


00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:32.400
Thank you for
not upsetting her.


00:38:32.700 --> 00:38:35.100
I assume you have
power of attorney.


00:38:35.200 --> 00:38:37.600
I thought this
case was closed.


00:38:37.900 --> 00:38:39.000
No. Just cold.


00:38:40.700 --> 00:38:42.500
What do you want, Chief Stone?


00:38:42.600 --> 00:38:44.300
Probably what you want.


00:38:44.800 --> 00:38:46.000
Justice for your sister.


00:38:46.100 --> 00:38:48.400
I'd like permissión
to exhume


00:38:48.700 --> 00:38:49.400
the body.


00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:51.700
My sister was cremated.


00:38:54.200 --> 00:38:54.800
Okay.


00:38:56.700 --> 00:38:57.400
This is old.


00:38:57.500 --> 00:38:59.100
I'm going to get
you a new pot.


00:38:59.200 --> 00:39:00.700
Did you see your
sister's body?


00:39:00.800 --> 00:39:04.500
No. Maybe my mother
wouldn't have had her stroke


00:39:05.300 --> 00:39:06.200
if I had been here.


00:39:06.300 --> 00:39:08.400
I wouldn't beat yourself up.


00:39:08.800 --> 00:39:11.100
You've obviously devoted
yourself to her.


00:39:11.200 --> 00:39:13.000
I left my job in L.A.,


00:39:13.400 --> 00:39:16.000
and I got her out
of that hospital,


00:39:16.100 --> 00:39:18.000
and we've been here ever since.


00:39:18.100 --> 00:39:19.800
Long way from Paradise.


00:39:21.900 --> 00:39:23.200
Too many memories.


00:39:24.700 --> 00:39:25.800
Do you have any


00:39:25.900 --> 00:39:29.000
personal effects of
your sister? Pictures?


00:39:29.200 --> 00:39:29.800
Why?


00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:31.400
Well, it's just
the way I work.


00:39:31.500 --> 00:39:32.800
Gives me a sense
of the person.


00:39:32.900 --> 00:39:34.000
Frankly, there's
not much in our files.


00:39:34.100 --> 00:39:38.100
We really don't want to open old
wounds unless there's a reason.


00:39:38.200 --> 00:39:40.400
Oh, I think there's a reason.


00:39:41.100 --> 00:39:45.100
Well, I got rid of all that
stuff after the funeral.


00:39:45.200 --> 00:39:47.100
It upset your mom?
Yeah.


00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:50.900
Frankly, it upset me, too.


00:39:53.300 --> 00:39:54.100
I'm sorry.


00:39:57.000 --> 00:39:58.900
This is going
to take a while.


00:39:59.000 --> 00:40:01.900
Do you still want coffee,
Chief Stone?


00:40:02.300 --> 00:40:03.000
Jesse.


00:40:04.100 --> 00:40:04.800
Jesse.


00:40:05.200 --> 00:40:06.800
Coffee would be good.


00:40:07.900 --> 00:40:09.600
It's a long way back.


00:40:22.200 --> 00:40:22.900
Jesse?


00:40:24.700 --> 00:40:26.600
Would you like
to eat at the bar?


00:40:26.700 --> 00:40:27.600
Sure, Laura.


00:40:28.600 --> 00:40:29.300
Okay.


00:40:32.800 --> 00:40:34.200
I thought I'd stop by,


00:40:34.300 --> 00:40:35.300
see if you need any help
fighting crime.


00:40:35.400 --> 00:40:39.200
What's happening at home
that you'd rather be here?


00:40:39.300 --> 00:40:40.200
Nothing.


00:40:40.500 --> 00:40:41.400
Not nothing.


00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:46.900
My wife's younger brother
is visiting with his wife.


00:40:48.100 --> 00:40:49.900
They have young children.


00:40:50.200 --> 00:40:52.800
You don't care
for young children?


00:40:52.900 --> 00:40:54.200
Neither of us do.


00:40:54.400 --> 00:40:56.000
But it's her brother.


00:40:56.100 --> 00:40:59.800
So your dropping by is not
all about helping me.


00:41:00.100 --> 00:41:01.600
It's nothing about that.


00:41:01.700 --> 00:41:03.000
Are you staying for dinner?


00:41:03.100 --> 00:41:05.700
Can I tell my wife
it's business?


00:41:05.900 --> 00:41:09.100
You can if you crank up
your lab for me.


00:41:09.600 --> 00:41:11.300
There's something
I want you to check.


00:41:11.400 --> 00:41:13.300
Can't Doc Perkins do it?


00:41:13.800 --> 00:41:16.600
I don't want to destroy
his confidence.


00:41:16.700 --> 00:41:19.700
Yeah, but State Homicide
operates on a budget.


00:41:19.800 --> 00:41:21.400
This stuff costs money.


00:41:21.500 --> 00:41:22.500
Is it important?


00:41:22.600 --> 00:41:23.800
I have no idea.


00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:29.300
Will you call
my wife for me?


00:41:30.500 --> 00:41:31.100
Okay.


00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:35.100
Then I'll crank up the lab.


00:41:37.300 --> 00:41:40.000
You know, marriage
is hard for cops.


00:41:40.100 --> 00:41:42.700
And the only people
we know how to talk to


00:41:42.800 --> 00:41:44.500
are the women we marry.


00:41:45.300 --> 00:41:47.400
Then the marriage breaks up,


00:41:47.500 --> 00:41:49.900
and you need to talk to someone,


00:41:50.100 --> 00:41:52.000
and only one you can't talk to


00:41:52.100 --> 00:41:54.000
is the woman you married.


00:41:54.300 --> 00:41:56.100
When did Molly call you?


00:41:58.200 --> 00:42:00.800
The morning
after you woke her up.


00:42:02.500 --> 00:42:05.900
Oh, Captain Healy will be
joining me for dinner, Laura.


00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:07.700
What can I get for you?


00:42:07.800 --> 00:42:09.400
Scotch on the rocks...


00:42:10.100 --> 00:42:11.600
and another for the Chief.


00:42:11.700 --> 00:42:12.900
I'm good, Laura.


00:42:26.400 --> 00:42:29.400
Have you talked
to the son of a bitch?


00:42:29.700 --> 00:42:30.300
No.


00:42:30.700 --> 00:42:34.000
But I will be talking
to the son of a bitch.


00:42:34.100 --> 00:42:35.000
Why'd Cathleen drop out


00:42:35.100 --> 00:42:38.000
of high school
before her senior year?


00:42:40.100 --> 00:42:43.100
What's that have to do
with her being raped?


00:42:43.200 --> 00:42:44.200
I don't know.


00:42:46.300 --> 00:42:49.000
I tried, but
she just wouldn't go.


00:42:49.300 --> 00:42:51.000
And I couldn't make her.


00:42:51.100 --> 00:42:52.300
I work all day.


00:42:52.700 --> 00:42:53.700
Her mom is...


00:42:53.800 --> 00:42:54.400
Gone.


00:42:55.200 --> 00:42:59.000
Took off with a guy
when Cathleen was just six...


00:43:00.900 --> 00:43:01.600
Look...


00:43:03.600 --> 00:43:05.300
I'm sorry, Chief Stone.


00:43:05.700 --> 00:43:08.300
This whole thing's
just got me...


00:43:09.200 --> 00:43:10.000
Pissed off?


00:43:14.600 --> 00:43:16.400
She came home very late.


00:43:18.400 --> 00:43:19.700
I confronted her.


00:43:20.900 --> 00:43:24.800
She got real upset,
and then it all just came out.


00:43:26.100 --> 00:43:28.200
Well, two things
you need to know.


00:43:28.300 --> 00:43:30.300
One is, I'm going to talk
to the son of a bitch.


00:43:30.400 --> 00:43:34.800
And two, you' re going to stay
away from the son of a bitch.


00:43:34.900 --> 00:43:35.800
Because?


00:43:36.300 --> 00:43:38.500
Because I'm the police chief.


00:44:04.800 --> 00:44:06.500
What were you thinking?


00:44:11.900 --> 00:44:12.600
Jesse!


00:44:15.200 --> 00:44:17.500
Boy, I do not get
many visitors.


00:44:17.600 --> 00:44:18.600
So how you doing, Hasty?


00:44:18.700 --> 00:44:21.500
Don't say "How you doing?"
to a convict.


00:44:21.600 --> 00:44:23.200
Okay, how's it going?


00:44:23.300 --> 00:44:26.500
Well, I teach
illiterate prisoners to read.


00:44:27.700 --> 00:44:30.600
I give financial advice
to the guards.


00:44:30.800 --> 00:44:32.500
How's the drinking thing?


00:44:32.600 --> 00:44:34.700
Better since I gave up hope.


00:44:36.300 --> 00:44:37.400
How's my wife?


00:44:38.600 --> 00:44:39.700
Ex-wife, Hasty.


00:44:40.300 --> 00:44:42.100
How's she doing?
Cissy?


00:44:42.200 --> 00:44:43.100
Is... Cissy.


00:44:44.200 --> 00:44:45.400
But she's okay?


00:44:47.200 --> 00:44:47.800
Yes.


00:44:48.100 --> 00:44:49.800
Jesse, you and Cissy...


00:44:52.700 --> 00:44:53.600
You never...


00:44:54.200 --> 00:44:55.200
No. We never.


00:44:59.500 --> 00:45:00.900
So, no hard feelings?


00:45:01.000 --> 00:45:02.900
Hey, a guy saves your life.


00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:05.300
Albeit for the wrong reasons...


00:45:06.300 --> 00:45:08.100
What are you doing here?


00:45:09.900 --> 00:45:12.100
Your bank was robbed in 1992.


00:45:13.200 --> 00:45:14.500
Teller was killed.


00:45:14.700 --> 00:45:16.100
Yeah, Rebecca. Nice kid.


00:45:16.200 --> 00:45:18.100
What do you remember about it?


00:45:18.200 --> 00:45:18.665
Nothing.


00:45:18.700 --> 00:45:21.300
Hasty, you can't be
put away twice


00:45:21.400 --> 00:45:22.300
for money laundering.


00:45:22.400 --> 00:45:23.400
I know that.
So?


00:45:23.500 --> 00:45:25.400
So I just didn't see anything.
Because?


00:45:25.500 --> 00:45:29.300
Because I was hiding
under my desk the whole time.


00:45:29.800 --> 00:45:33.400
There were no surveillance
cameras in your bank.


00:45:34.200 --> 00:45:35.000
Small town.


00:45:35.400 --> 00:45:37.800
Were you laundering money
for Gino Fish back then?


00:45:37.900 --> 00:45:38.800
No.


00:45:41.300 --> 00:45:43.400
No, on my sacred honor, no.


00:45:46.900 --> 00:45:49.500
You know, Hasty, when I
said you saved my life,


00:45:49.600 --> 00:45:52.800
I wasn't talking about the night
I arrested you.


00:45:52.900 --> 00:45:56.500
I meant you saved my life
because you hired me.


00:45:57.400 --> 00:45:59.200
Albeit for the wrong reasons.


00:45:59.300 --> 00:46:01.500
I'm very fond of you, Jesse.


00:46:04.600 --> 00:46:05.700
See you, Hasty.


00:46:17.900 --> 00:46:18.500
Suit.


00:46:18.900 --> 00:46:19.500
Jesse!


00:46:20.100 --> 00:46:21.400
Where have you
been, Skipper?


00:46:21.500 --> 00:46:22.200
Fighting crime.


00:46:22.300 --> 00:46:24.600
Rose at the
orthodontist again?


00:46:25.200 --> 00:46:25.800
Yes.


00:46:26.900 --> 00:46:28.000
How you feeling?


00:46:28.100 --> 00:46:28.765
Perfect.


00:46:28.800 --> 00:46:30.700
You lost a little weight.


00:46:32.000 --> 00:46:33.200
I'm not much good


00:46:33.300 --> 00:46:34.500
with the phones.


00:46:35.200 --> 00:46:36.300
You supposed to be here?


00:46:36.400 --> 00:46:37.500
They let me out of the hospital.


00:46:37.600 --> 00:46:40.100
They say it was okay for you
to go back to work?


00:46:40.200 --> 00:46:40.900
I didn't ask.


00:46:41.000 --> 00:46:43.900
Well, I need you
to answer the phones


00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:46.300
for now, Suitcase.


00:46:46.400 --> 00:46:48.500
How do you feel about that?


00:46:48.800 --> 00:46:50.100
I don't like it.


00:46:50.400 --> 00:46:51.800
I feel fine, Lieu.


00:46:53.700 --> 00:46:54.300
Okay.


00:47:03.700 --> 00:47:05.600
Boy, that thing's a mess.


00:47:06.100 --> 00:47:06.800
Tell me about it.


00:47:06.900 --> 00:47:08.700
The folder's torn.
The pictures are dirty.


00:47:08.800 --> 00:47:09.800
The papers are all wrinkled...


00:47:09.900 --> 00:47:11.600
Well, I threw it
across the room.


00:47:11.700 --> 00:47:12.700
Why'd you do that?


00:47:12.800 --> 00:47:14.400
Because it's a mess.


00:47:17.200 --> 00:47:19.300
I think DeAngelo wants your job.


00:47:19.400 --> 00:47:20.700
I feel it in my cells.


00:47:20.800 --> 00:47:22.000
Well, actually, he thinks


00:47:22.100 --> 00:47:25.000
he should have had the job
to begin with.


00:47:25.100 --> 00:47:27.400
I'd like to help you
with your drug case.


00:47:27.500 --> 00:47:32.200
Suit, do you remember anything
about your stay at the hospital?


00:47:32.700 --> 00:47:33.300
No.


00:47:34.100 --> 00:47:34.600
Okay...


00:47:35.100 --> 00:47:37.300
What did you think
about the bank robbery?


00:47:37.400 --> 00:47:38.500
I think you' re on to something.


00:47:38.600 --> 00:47:40.000
Rose doesn't think so.


00:47:40.100 --> 00:47:41.900
Rose hasn't been in the field.


00:47:42.000 --> 00:47:43.400
Well, she threw up.


00:47:43.700 --> 00:47:44.700
Was she sick?


00:47:45.100 --> 00:47:46.500
It's not important.


00:47:47.000 --> 00:47:50.300
You know, I think
we should check for blood


00:47:50.700 --> 00:47:52.800
on those clothes
you found.


00:47:53.100 --> 00:47:57.200
You know, there might be
an upside to this coma thing.


00:47:57.800 --> 00:47:58.900
What are you talking about?


00:47:59.000 --> 00:48:01.400
You know what I'm talking about.


00:48:03.800 --> 00:48:04.600
You mean...


00:48:06.000 --> 00:48:06.600
Yes.


00:48:07.700 --> 00:48:08.700
Cop intuition.


00:48:09.000 --> 00:48:11.300
Now you' re as crazy as I am.


00:48:23.100 --> 00:48:24.300
Watch your step.


00:48:29.800 --> 00:48:31.500
Well... Inspector Yokel.


00:48:32.300 --> 00:48:34.200
Actually it's Chief Yokel.


00:48:35.300 --> 00:48:36.200
Where's your badge?


00:48:36.300 --> 00:48:37.700
It's in a drawer.


00:48:38.300 --> 00:48:39.000
Ah...


00:48:39.500 --> 00:48:40.300
This your boat?


00:48:40.400 --> 00:48:43.300
Why, you don't think I could
afford a boat like this?


00:48:43.400 --> 00:48:45.000
The Lady Jane's mine.


00:48:45.800 --> 00:48:46.900
I'm Chief Stone.


00:48:47.000 --> 00:48:48.900
This is Officer Gammon.
I'm Harrison.


00:48:49.000 --> 00:48:50.800
Nice to meet you,
Mr. Harrison.


00:48:50.900 --> 00:48:52.400
Harrison is my first name.


00:48:52.500 --> 00:48:53.700
I'm Harrison Pendleton.


00:48:53.800 --> 00:48:54.400
I see.


00:48:55.500 --> 00:48:56.300
Nice boat.


00:48:56.900 --> 00:48:57.700
Schooner.


00:48:58.800 --> 00:49:02.800
Officer Gammon would like
to ask you a few questions.


00:49:07.700 --> 00:49:10.000
Do you know a Cathleen Holton?


00:49:10.900 --> 00:49:11.500
I do.


00:49:12.600 --> 00:49:14.600
Was she a guest
on your schooner?


00:49:14.700 --> 00:49:15.500
Yes.
When?


00:49:16.700 --> 00:49:17.400
Four days ago.


00:49:17.500 --> 00:49:20.300
She joined some friends and me
for an evening cruise.


00:49:20.400 --> 00:49:22.300
Do you know how old she is?!


00:49:22.400 --> 00:49:24.600
Yes. 18 years and two months.


00:49:25.800 --> 00:49:27.400
She showed me her ID.


00:49:29.100 --> 00:49:31.800
I was wondering
if you could show me below.


00:49:31.900 --> 00:49:33.600
Do you have a warrant?


00:49:33.900 --> 00:49:34.500
No.


00:49:36.000 --> 00:49:37.100
Well, then, no.


00:49:42.400 --> 00:49:44.300
Guy's got two last names.


00:49:44.600 --> 00:49:46.700
You might have briefed me
that I was going


00:49:46.800 --> 00:49:47.900
to question the suspect.


00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:49.800
Well, I'm not sure
he's a suspect.


00:49:49.900 --> 00:49:52.700
But I thought
you handled it well...


00:49:52.800 --> 00:49:54.600
till you got pissed off.


00:49:57.900 --> 00:50:00.400
Jesse, why don't you get
a cell phone?


00:50:00.500 --> 00:50:01.900
' Cause I don't like them.


00:50:02.000 --> 00:50:03.200
You can always page me.


00:50:03.300 --> 00:50:04.500
I have.
Well...


00:50:05.700 --> 00:50:07.300
call me
on the car radio.


00:50:07.400 --> 00:50:07.865
I have.


00:50:07.900 --> 00:50:10.000
You've been spending
a lot of time


00:50:10.100 --> 00:50:11.500
away from the office.


00:50:11.600 --> 00:50:12.300
I have.


00:50:12.700 --> 00:50:13.300
At home?


00:50:14.400 --> 00:50:14.700
No.


00:50:16.300 --> 00:50:16.900
Good.


00:50:18.500 --> 00:50:20.300
So, I assume
you've talked


00:50:20.400 --> 00:50:21.800
to the bank guard.


00:50:22.600 --> 00:50:23.200
I did.


00:50:24.200 --> 00:50:25.300
Have you talked to the mother?


00:50:25.400 --> 00:50:26.800
Actually, I didn't.


00:50:29.800 --> 00:50:31.200
What are you doing?


00:50:45.100 --> 00:50:46.200
Run that plate.


00:51:01.100 --> 00:51:03.500
License and
registration, please.


00:51:05.800 --> 00:51:08.400
Did I do something
wrong, Officer?


00:51:08.700 --> 00:51:11.100
You have no front
license plate,


00:51:11.900 --> 00:51:12.700
Mr. Genest.


00:51:14.800 --> 00:51:16.100
I knew someone named Genest.


00:51:16.200 --> 00:51:17.000
Joe Genest?


00:51:18.400 --> 00:51:19.300
He your brother?


00:51:19.400 --> 00:51:20.800
He was my brother.


00:51:23.300 --> 00:51:24.300
I tell you what.


00:51:24.400 --> 00:51:27.000
I'm going to let you off
on the license plate.


00:51:27.100 --> 00:51:28.200
Just put one on.


00:51:28.300 --> 00:51:29.700
Thank you, Officer.


00:51:30.300 --> 00:51:31.400
One more thing.


00:51:33.200 --> 00:51:35.500
Don't follow me around, Terry.


00:59:46.600 --> 00:59:47.200
Hello.


00:59:47.900 --> 00:59:48.800
Jesse Stone.


00:59:48.900 --> 00:59:49.600
Oh, I, I checked in storage


00:59:49.700 --> 00:59:52.300
and I couldn't find anything
that might help you.


00:59:52.400 --> 00:59:53.400
I'm so sorry.


00:59:55.400 --> 00:59:57.500
It's like she didn't exist.


00:59:58.400 --> 00:59:59.900
Regrets, Chief Stone.


01:00:00.600 --> 01:00:01.200
Jesse.


01:00:02.700 --> 01:00:03.500
Jesse...


01:00:05.600 --> 01:00:08.700
Listen, um...
I know this is forward, um,


01:00:10.700 --> 01:00:13.100
but if you' re ever around here,


01:00:15.100 --> 01:00:15.900
I'd love to see you again.


01:00:16.000 --> 01:00:20.300
Well, if you' re ever in
Paradise, I'd love to see you.


01:00:20.600 --> 01:00:21.200
Ah...


01:00:23.100 --> 01:00:23.900
well, um...


01:00:25.000 --> 01:00:28.500
I can't get that far away
from my mom, so...


01:00:28.600 --> 01:00:30.800
I guess we' re at an impasse.


01:00:31.400 --> 01:00:32.200
Not really.


01:00:35.600 --> 01:00:36.200
Thanks.


01:00:37.500 --> 01:00:38.800
Thanks.


01:00:39.200 --> 01:00:42.900
And the woman there said
we should have T-shirts


01:00:43.400 --> 01:00:45.900
that say
"I went hunting here"...


01:01:14.400 --> 01:01:17.400
It looks like she was having
a pretty good time stripping.


01:01:17.500 --> 01:01:20.800
Cathleen is apparently wise
beyond her years


01:01:22.000 --> 01:01:25.100
and in my expert
police chief's opinion,


01:01:25.800 --> 01:01:28.900
it hardly looks
like she was being raped.


01:01:29.200 --> 01:01:31.000
Where did you get these?


01:01:31.100 --> 01:01:33.000
I accidentally found them.


01:01:33.700 --> 01:01:34.600
Where did you find them?


01:01:34.700 --> 01:01:37.900
In a cabinet below decks
on the Lady Jane.


01:01:38.900 --> 01:01:41.100
I'd be interested
to know what you think.


01:01:41.200 --> 01:01:43.300
Do you think I should
see them, Jesse?


01:01:43.400 --> 01:01:44.000
No.


01:02:20.700 --> 01:02:22.800
Are you happy in your work?


01:02:23.900 --> 01:02:25.200
What do you mean?


01:02:25.900 --> 01:02:28.700
Well, there's this
Japanese prison camp commander


01:02:28.800 --> 01:02:29.700
in Bridge on the River Kwai


01:02:29.800 --> 01:02:33.600
and he just keeps telling these
miserable starving prisoners,


01:02:33.700 --> 01:02:35.600
"Be happy
in your work."


01:02:37.400 --> 01:02:39.300
You didn't see the movie.


01:02:40.200 --> 01:02:42.400
You happy in your work,
Cathleen?


01:02:42.500 --> 01:02:43.700
What are you talking about?


01:02:43.800 --> 01:02:49.100
The point I was attempting
to make is this is a lousy job.


01:02:50.500 --> 01:02:52.700
You need some help with that?


01:02:52.800 --> 01:02:53.400
No.


01:02:58.700 --> 01:03:01.700
Why'd you drop out
of school, Cathleen?


01:03:02.200 --> 01:03:03.500
Why are you here?


01:03:04.600 --> 01:03:05.400
You miss your mom?


01:03:05.500 --> 01:03:07.800
You've been checking up on me.


01:03:08.600 --> 01:03:09.365
I have.


01:03:09.400 --> 01:03:13.500
Don't talk to me about things
you don't know anything about.


01:03:13.600 --> 01:03:16.400
Actually,
I know something about that.


01:03:16.900 --> 01:03:18.200
Your mom run off?


01:03:19.000 --> 01:03:21.600
No, she died...
when I was eight.


01:03:24.000 --> 01:03:25.700
I miss my mom
a lot.


01:03:26.600 --> 01:03:28.000
Moms are important.


01:03:28.100 --> 01:03:31.500
Well, you don't miss
someone you never knew.


01:03:32.000 --> 01:03:35.000
You know how to do
hospital corners, Chief Stone?


01:03:35.100 --> 01:03:35.700
I do.


01:03:36.700 --> 01:03:41.000
And call me Jesse now
that you' re 18 and all grown up.


01:03:41.200 --> 01:03:42.800
What's that supposed to mean?


01:03:42.900 --> 01:03:44.000
It means
you' re not


01:03:44.100 --> 01:03:45.200
a kid anymore.


01:03:45.800 --> 01:03:47.900
It means you' re fair game.


01:03:48.600 --> 01:03:49.800
I saw the tape.


01:03:51.200 --> 01:03:51.665
So?


01:03:51.700 --> 01:03:55.800
It didn't look like anybody made
you take off your clothes.


01:03:55.900 --> 01:03:56.465
So?


01:03:56.500 --> 01:03:58.500
That's no excuse
for what he did.


01:03:58.600 --> 01:04:00.200
There's another tape.


01:04:01.100 --> 01:04:03.200
Just you
and Mr. Pendleton.


01:04:07.600 --> 01:04:10.500
He had a hidden camera
in his bedroom.


01:04:19.600 --> 01:04:21.600
I want you to tell your dad.


01:04:21.700 --> 01:04:22.700
Why should I?


01:04:24.600 --> 01:04:25.300
Because he loves you,


01:04:25.400 --> 01:04:28.400
and I don't want to see your dad
do something stupid.


01:04:28.500 --> 01:04:30.200
Unintended consequences.


01:04:31.300 --> 01:04:35.000
You' re not supposed to be here.


01:04:35.035 --> 01:04:35.665
No, I'm not.


01:04:35.700 --> 01:04:38.500
You' re not supposed to try and
talk me out of this, are you?


01:04:38.600 --> 01:04:39.700
That's correct.


01:04:41.000 --> 01:04:43.000
I could get you in trouble.


01:04:43.100 --> 01:04:43.765
You could.


01:04:43.800 --> 01:04:46.800
You don't think
what he did was wrong?


01:04:47.400 --> 01:04:50.200
It was wrong,
but it wasn't illegal.


01:04:51.900 --> 01:04:53.200
Yeah, but he's...


01:04:53.300 --> 01:04:54.100
A grownup?


01:04:55.600 --> 01:04:56.900
You know
what I think?


01:04:57.000 --> 01:04:58.800
I think you
don't like yourself


01:04:58.900 --> 01:05:00.800
so much for what you did.


01:05:01.000 --> 01:05:01.700
I think you love your dad


01:05:01.800 --> 01:05:04.400
and you know how disappointed
he'd be if he knew the truth,


01:05:04.500 --> 01:05:07.100
but you getting even
with some sick son of a bitch


01:05:07.200 --> 01:05:08.900
isn't going to change
any of that.


01:05:09.000 --> 01:05:11.800
Well, at least,
then he won't do it again.


01:05:11.900 --> 01:05:13.600
Oh, he'll do it again.


01:05:13.900 --> 01:05:14.600
Why?


01:05:15.000 --> 01:05:16.000
Because he can.


01:05:16.100 --> 01:05:19.200
And there's nothing
you or I can do to stop him.


01:05:19.300 --> 01:05:20.100
You know...


01:05:22.500 --> 01:05:25.200
you live long enough,
you have regrets.


01:05:25.300 --> 01:05:27.700
And the ones
that nag at you the most


01:05:27.800 --> 01:05:31.300
are the ones where you knew
you had a choice,


01:05:31.500 --> 01:05:35.200
the ones where you knew you
could have stopped yourself,


01:05:35.300 --> 01:05:37.400
the ones where
you looked into the mirror


01:05:37.500 --> 01:05:39.900
and everything good
inside you said,


01:05:40.000 --> 01:05:41.200
"Don't do this."


01:05:46.200 --> 01:05:49.700
You go talk to your dad and I'll
go punch him in the mouth.


01:05:49.800 --> 01:05:50.700
How's that?


01:06:21.000 --> 01:06:22.400
The Paradise Motel.


01:06:22.900 --> 01:06:24.100
I know it well.


01:06:24.300 --> 01:06:25.000
As do I.


01:06:25.300 --> 01:06:26.900
I used to live there.


01:06:27.300 --> 01:06:30.900
You' re not following me around,
are you, Terry?


01:06:31.100 --> 01:06:32.400
I prefer Terence.


01:06:32.700 --> 01:06:34.100
And I prefer you didn't do that.


01:06:34.200 --> 01:06:35.100
Do what?


01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:37.400
Follow me around, Terry.


01:06:37.500 --> 01:06:38.900
Are you trying to provoke me?


01:06:39.000 --> 01:06:42.000
I was going
to ask you the same thing.


01:06:42.100 --> 01:06:44.500
I'm just sitting here
reading the paper.


01:06:44.600 --> 01:06:47.500
Did you get that license plate
fixed, Terry?


01:06:47.600 --> 01:06:49.100
Yes, I did, Officer.


01:06:49.300 --> 01:06:52.100
And since now I have a
violation-free motor vehicle,


01:06:52.200 --> 01:06:54.100
I'll drive it wherever I want.


01:06:54.200 --> 01:06:56.400
I'll obey all traffic
regulations


01:06:56.500 --> 01:06:58.500
so as you can't harass me,


01:06:58.800 --> 01:07:00.200
unless you set me up,


01:07:00.300 --> 01:07:02.800
the way you did my brother
when you killed him.


01:07:02.900 --> 01:07:05.500
I didn't kill your brother,
Terry,


01:07:06.000 --> 01:07:08.600
but I did set him up
pretty good.


01:07:17.700 --> 01:07:18.900
God, I miss her.


01:07:23.700 --> 01:07:24.400
Scotch?


01:07:24.600 --> 01:07:25.600
For the lady.


01:07:26.200 --> 01:07:27.000
Thank you.


01:07:28.900 --> 01:07:29.700
Thank you.


01:07:31.200 --> 01:07:32.300
Long way back?


01:07:35.900 --> 01:07:36.700
It is.


01:07:37.200 --> 01:07:38.500
Thanks for meeting me halfway.


01:07:38.600 --> 01:07:42.200
Well, actually, it's three
quarters to one quarter,


01:07:42.300 --> 01:07:44.000
so I guess you owe me.


01:07:46.100 --> 01:07:50.000
Are you going to find the man
who killed my sister?


01:07:51.900 --> 01:07:53.300
Well, it's been 15 years.


01:07:53.400 --> 01:07:55.100
How long have
you been on it?


01:07:55.200 --> 01:07:56.000
Three days.


01:07:56.200 --> 01:07:59.100
That's not actually
why I called you.


01:07:59.300 --> 01:08:00.700
Why'd you call me?


01:08:01.300 --> 01:08:04.400
The soup of the day
is cream of tomato.


01:08:05.000 --> 01:08:05.800
Thank you.


01:08:10.500 --> 01:08:12.500
You know, I wasn't
being entirely honest


01:08:12.600 --> 01:08:13.900
