01:12:35.200 --> 01:12:36.000
Exactly.


01:12:37.100 --> 01:12:37.700
So...


01:12:39.200 --> 01:12:40.600
did I answer your question?


01:12:40.700 --> 01:12:42.800
Oh, I think I know the answer.


01:12:42.900 --> 01:12:45.500
I just wanted
to be sure you did.


01:12:46.000 --> 01:12:47.500
I want you
out of my town.


01:12:47.600 --> 01:12:49.300
Your town?
That's right.


01:12:49.400 --> 01:12:51.300
What are you, the sheriff?


01:12:52.300 --> 01:12:52.665
Chief Stone?


01:12:52.700 --> 01:12:54.300
Hey, I'm just here
for field training.


01:12:54.400 --> 01:12:56.400
I'm missing some
personal property.


01:12:56.500 --> 01:12:59.200
Did you misplace
the item or items?


01:12:59.800 --> 01:13:01.300
I think it was stolen.


01:13:01.400 --> 01:13:02.100
I see.


01:13:02.700 --> 01:13:03.400
A theft.


01:13:03.600 --> 01:13:04.400
Well, during
your abbreviated


01:13:04.500 --> 01:13:07.200
stay in Paradise,
we aim to protect and serve,


01:13:07.300 --> 01:13:10.700
so, just what are you missing,
Mr. Pendleton?


01:13:11.800 --> 01:13:14.600
Uh, perhaps I did
misplace the items.


01:13:16.400 --> 01:13:17.100
How's tomorrow?


01:13:17.200 --> 01:13:18.600
How's after the race?


01:13:18.700 --> 01:13:19.800
How's tomorrow?


01:13:23.300 --> 01:13:24.000
Oh, well.


01:13:24.900 --> 01:13:25.900
Mr. Pendleton?


01:13:26.400 --> 01:13:27.100
Yes?


01:13:27.900 --> 01:13:28.900
Shame on you.


01:13:33.900 --> 01:13:34.800
How'd I do?


01:13:35.200 --> 01:13:37.000
Officially, I'm shocked.


01:13:37.100 --> 01:13:37.900
Unofficially.


01:13:38.000 --> 01:13:39.100
I'm proud of you.


01:13:39.200 --> 01:13:40.800
What would you have done,
Jesse?


01:13:40.900 --> 01:13:42.800
I would have
slugged him.


01:13:48.800 --> 01:13:50.400
Skipper, what happened?


01:13:50.700 --> 01:13:51.400
I fell.


01:13:51.500 --> 01:13:52.300
Where'


01:13:52.700 --> 01:13:53.500
Orthodontist.


01:13:53.600 --> 01:13:54.700
Where's Suit?
Market.


01:13:54.800 --> 01:13:56.000
He said to let you know


01:13:56.100 --> 01:13:58.100
that Captain
Healy called.


01:13:58.500 --> 01:13:59.400
Hey, Skipper,


01:13:59.700 --> 01:14:03.300
do you think I could have
the day off tomorrow?


01:14:12.000 --> 01:14:15.300
Are Gino Fish and his
receptionist an item?


01:14:15.700 --> 01:14:17.200
You got a problem
with that?


01:14:17.300 --> 01:14:19.600
Hey, I'm just
accumulating data.


01:14:19.700 --> 01:14:21.800
Your in-laws
still visiting?


01:14:21.900 --> 01:14:23.600
That's what they call it.


01:14:23.700 --> 01:14:26.600
What did you find out
about Terry Genest?


01:14:26.700 --> 01:14:28.200
Well, he prefers Terence.


01:14:28.300 --> 01:14:29.600
Just got out of prison.


01:14:29.700 --> 01:14:30.900
Freelance gunsel.


01:14:31.100 --> 01:14:33.200
Works for Gino
on occasión.


01:14:33.400 --> 01:14:34.800
Bit of a
loose cannon.


01:14:34.900 --> 01:14:35.700
Cokehead.


01:14:35.800 --> 01:14:37.500
You better be a
little careful.


01:14:37.600 --> 01:14:38.300
Everybody says that.


01:14:38.400 --> 01:14:42.000
The material on the robber's
clothes was blood.


01:14:43.400 --> 01:14:45.900
Now, we' re no going to get
much more out of it.


01:14:46.000 --> 01:14:47.400
It was pretty degraded.


01:14:47.500 --> 01:14:48.600
Oh, and I also, uh,


01:14:48.700 --> 01:14:52.000
