Suitcase said you wanted.


01:14:52.100 --> 01:14:52.700
And?


01:14:53.100 --> 01:14:53.665
Dead end.


01:14:53.700 --> 01:14:57.600
There were no accidental
gunshot wounds in May ' 92.


01:14:58.800 --> 01:15:01.900
I also checked, uh, New
Hampshire and Rhode Island.


01:15:02.000 --> 01:15:03.300
You' re thorough.


01:15:03.500 --> 01:15:04.100
I am.


01:15:04.400 --> 01:15:07.800
And I don't know what
this other thing's about.


01:15:07.900 --> 01:15:08.800
Is he okay?


01:15:09.100 --> 01:15:13.500
He's not quite in the same pond
with the other ducks yet.


01:15:13.900 --> 01:15:15.200
What "other thing"?


01:15:15.300 --> 01:15:16.300
Well, he wanted me to, uh,


01:15:16.400 --> 01:15:20.400
run a background check on
L.A. resident Leeann Lewis.


01:15:21.100 --> 01:15:21.800
Because?


01:15:23.600 --> 01:15:25.000
He said he had a feeling.


01:15:25.100 --> 01:15:27.600
He's been having
a lot of those.


01:15:29.500 --> 01:15:31.200
Uh, the only thing
we got was


01:15:31.300 --> 01:15:32.500
she was reported
missing once.


01:15:32.600 --> 01:15:34.600
Landlady filed
the report.


01:15:34.700 --> 01:15:37.500
Well, she left
to take care of her mom.


01:15:37.600 --> 01:15:39.200
Anyway, it went away.


01:15:39.700 --> 01:15:43.100
And she sent the landlady
an apology and money


01:15:43.200 --> 01:15:44.300
to pay off the lease.


01:15:44.400 --> 01:15:45.800
And that was May ' 92.


01:15:45.900 --> 01:15:47.000
You mean ' 94.


01:15:47.300 --> 01:15:48.000
No...


01:15:49.700 --> 01:15:52.600
she was reported missing
May 23, 1992.


01:15:53.500 --> 01:15:54.700
That's the, uh,


01:15:54.800 --> 01:15:57.400
that's the same date
as the robbery.


01:15:57.500 --> 01:15:58.800
Is that important?


01:15:59.800 --> 01:16:00.400
Jesse?


01:16:03.400 --> 01:16:05.700
